  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s interests in a peaceful, stable and prosperous Indo-Pacific are advanced by improving development outcomes in the Pacific region, including social inclusion. The Australia-Pacific Partnerships Platform (AusP3) provides a suite of flexible, fit-for-purpose development services to Nauru, Kiribati and Tuvalu, with support also provided in 2023 to Federated States of Micronesia (FSM), the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI) and the Cook Islands. In 2023, AusP3 finalised its Gender Equality, Disability and Social Inclusion (GEDSI) strategy for mainstreaming GEDSI into AusP3&#x2019;s activities. This included support to analyse GEDSI inequalities and incorporate actions to address these into AusP3 personnel workplans. For example, in Nauru and Kiribati, AusP3 personnel tracked gender-related spending in national budgets. In Tuvalu, AusP3 supported the Education Department to implement its policy on inclusive education. In FSM, AusP3&#x2019;s advisory support enabled the Chuuk Department of Education to implement its Child Protection Policy.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical support to the Planning and Aid Division within the Ministry of Finance is playing a significant role in promoting more effective public sector management in Nauru. A more cohesive approach to planning and aid was evident with the completion of the first annual report against the Nauru National Sustainable Development Strategy, with the support of the Planning and Aid Adviser deployed through the Australian Pacific Partnership Platform. An &#x2018;aid-in-kind&#x2019; data capturing system was developed for Nauru Development Fund reporting, and the Planning and Aid Division is also increasingly effective in supporting Ministerial requests for donor support.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
